<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Subroutine Calls]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R01_Inputs,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R02_StateTransitions,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R03_StateLogic,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R10_Global,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R20_Alarms,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R01_Inputs" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Logic inputs

*Replace always off bits with real conditions

JARVIS INFERENCE: the Supervisor program was never exported. Safety OK is aggregated here from the safety relay and air pressure; a real machine adds gate switches, light curtains muted status, etc.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(i_SafetyRelayOK)XIC(i_AirPressureOK)OTE(SafetyOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Manual Mode Select]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_ManualMode)OTE(ManualMode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Fault Reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(i_FaultResetPB) ,XIC(HMI_Momentary.2) ]OTE(FaultReset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Stations In Auto Mode

*Add one contact per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.q_AutoMode)XIC(\S01_PartLoad.q_AutoMode)XIC(\S05_ServoPNP.q_AutoMode)OTE(AllStationsInAuto);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start OK - All Stations Ready To Start

*Add one contact per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.q_StartOK)XIC(\S01_PartLoad.q_StartOK)XIC(\S05_ServoPNP.q_StartOK)OTE(StartOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Stations Stopped

*Add one contact per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.q_AutoStopped)XIC(\S01_PartLoad.q_AutoStopped)XIC(\S05_ServoPNP.q_AutoStopped)OTE(AllStationsStopped);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Any Station Fault Active]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.q_AlarmActive) ,XIC(\S01_PartLoad.q_AlarmActive) ,XIC(\S05_ServoPNP.q_AlarmActive) ]OTE(AnyStationFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Any Station Warning Active]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.q_WarningActive) ,XIC(\S01_PartLoad.q_WarningActive) ,XIC(\S05_ServoPNP.q_WarningActive) ]OTE(AnyStationWarning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cycle Start Request]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(i_CycleStartPB) ,XIC(HMI_Momentary.0) ]OTE(CycleStartRequest);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cycle Stop Request]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(i_CycleStopPB) ,XIC(HMI_Momentary.1) ]OTE(CycleStopRequest);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear HMI Manual Triggers]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_MomentaryOnPrevScan)MOVE(0,HMI_Momentary);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(HMI_Momentary,0)OTE(HMI_MomentaryOnPrevScan);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R02_StateTransitions" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start Of State Machine

JARVIS INFERENCE: the Supervisor state map below mirrors the station template grammar (0=Safety Stop, 1=Manual, 2=Idle Not Ready, 3=Idle Ready, sequence on the +3 grid, 127=Fault). The real Supervisor state numbering is unconfirmed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 2: Auto mode idle not ready]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Status.State[0]) XIC(SafetyOK) ,XIC(Status.State[1]) XIO(ManualMode) ,XIC(Status.State[3]) XIO(StartOK) ,XIC(Status.State[127]) XIO(q_AlarmActive) XIO(AnyStationFault) ]MOVE(2,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 3: Auto mode idle ready]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Status.State[2]) ,XIC(Status.State[10]) XIO(q_CycleStartLatch) ]XIC(AllStationsInAuto)XIC(StartOK)XIO(ManualMode)MOVE(3,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 4: Cycle running]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[3])XIC(q_CycleStartLatch)MOVE(4,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 7: Cycle stopping - wait for all stations to finish their current cycle

JARVIS INFERENCE: CycleStopping is implied by the station R01 pattern (XIO of q_CycleStartLatch drives CycleStopping locally); the Supervisor holds this state until every station reports q_AutoStopped.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[4])XIO(q_CycleStartLatch)MOVE(7,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 10: Cycle stopped]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[7])XIC(AllStationsStopped)MOVE(10,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cycle Start Latch

JARVIS INFERENCE: latch requires idle-ready, no faults, and a start request. Recovery/retry bias: a station warning does NOT block a start.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[3])XIC(CycleStartRequest)XIC(StartOK)XIO(AnyStationFault)XIO(q_AlarmActive)OTL(q_CycleStartLatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cycle Start Unlatch

JARVIS INFERENCE: the machine cycle-stops on operator request, manual mode, safety loss, any fault, or batch complete. QUESTION FOR LEADS: should a single-station fault unlatch the whole machine, or should the machine pause and let the station recover?]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(CycleStopRequest) ,XIC(ManualMode) ,XIO(SafetyOK) ,XIC(q_AlarmActive) ,XIC(AnyStationFault) ,XIC(\Tracking.q_BatchComplete) ]OTU(q_CycleStartLatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 127: Fault

JARVIS INFERENCE: only Supervisor-level alarms (safety, air) fault the Supervisor itself. Station faults stop the cycle but are owned by the station programs - machines that stop less.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(q_AlarmActive)MOVE(127,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 1: Manual Mode]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(ManualMode)MOVE(1,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State 0: Safety Stop]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(SafetyOK) ,XIC(S:FS) ]MOVE(0,Control.StateReg);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[State Engine]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[State_Engine_128Max(StateEngine,Control,Status,StateHistory);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Cycle Time

Evidence: X-drive Rungs\Machine Cycle Time\CycleTime.L5X. Index complete one-shot derived from the indexer arriving on station.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(\S00_IndexerSP.p_OnStation)ONS(ONS.4)OTE(IndexComplete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Stop Reason (V4.1 - Supervisor R02 rung 13)

JARVIS INFERENCE: V4.1 added q_MachineStopReason and rungs 13-14 to R02_StateTransitions. The reason-code map is reconstructed: 1=Operator 2=Manual Mode 3=Safety 4=Fault 5=Batch Complete.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[4])[XIC(CycleStopRequest) MOVE(1,q_MachineStopReason) ,XIC(ManualMode) MOVE(2,q_MachineStopReason) ,XIO(SafetyOK) MOVE(3,q_MachineStopReason) ,[XIC(q_AlarmActive) ,XIC(AnyStationFault) ] MOVE(4,q_MachineStopReason) ,XIC(\Tracking.q_BatchComplete) MOVE(5,q_MachineStopReason) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear Stop Reason On New Cycle Start (V4.1 - Supervisor R02 rung 14)

JARVIS INFERENCE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[3])XIC(q_CycleStartLatch)ONS(ONS.5)MOVE(0,q_MachineStopReason);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R03_StateLogic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output Status To Stations

Evidence: every station R01_Inputs maps these five outputs 1:1 (q_ManualMode, q_SafetyOK, q_FaultReset, q_CycleStartLatch, q_CycleStopped).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[1])OTE(q_ManualMode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(SafetyOK)OTE(q_SafetyOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(FaultReset)OTE(q_FaultReset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cycle Stopped - stations one-shot this to clear CycleRunning

JARVIS INFERENCE on state set: stopped = anything except running/stopping.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Status.State[0]) ,XIC(Status.State[1]) ,XIC(Status.State[2]) ,XIC(Status.State[3]) ,XIC(Status.State[10]) ,XIC(Status.State[127]) ]OTE(q_CycleStopped);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Running - consumed by Alarms (stop-fault capture), Production (runtime), and cycle-time rungs

JARVIS INFERENCE: running includes Cycle Stopping so the stop-fault capture in \Alarms rung 13 can see the fault that ended the cycle.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Status.State[4]) ,XIC(Status.State[7]) ]OTE(q_MachineRunning);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Fault Active - any Supervisor or station fault]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(q_AlarmActive) ,XIC(AnyStationFault) ]OTE(q_MachineFaultActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Cycle Time Capture

Evidence: X-drive Rungs\Machine Cycle Time\CycleTime.L5X (verbatim pattern).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(IndexComplete)[DIV(CycleTimer.ACC,1000,p_CycleTime) ,MovingAverage(MovingAverageA,p_CycleTime,25) ,MovingAverage(MovingAverageB,p_CycleTime,100) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(q_MachineRunning)XIO(IndexComplete)TON(CycleTimer,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Light Stack Control

JARVIS RECONSTRUCTION: the Light Stack Control AOI exists per Revision History (V4.0 fix, V4.1 HornOverride input) but was never exported. Interface and logic are reconstructed for review.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LightStackControl(LightStack,q_MachineRunning,q_MachineFaultActive,AnyStationWarning,StartOK,ManualMode,SafetyOK,HMI_HornOverride,g_MachineBasic.Flash500msPD,q_GreenLight,q_AmberLight,q_RedLight,q_CycleStartLight,q_AlarmHorn);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R10_Global" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Global Machine Basics

JARVIS INFERENCE: some machine-level routine must drive g_MachineBasic and g_CPUDateTime - no template exports it. Placed in Supervisor R10_Global for review; the leads may keep it in a dedicated program or the MainRoutine.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTE(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOn);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOn)OTE(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOff);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[PLC Power Up Complete]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOn)TON(PowerUpDelay,?,?)XIC(PowerUpDelay.DN)OTE(g_MachineBasic.PowerUpCP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[EIP Motion Power Up Complete

*Replace the delay with MotionGroup.GroupSynced on servo machines]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.PowerUpCP)TON(MotionUpDelay,?,?)XIC(MotionUpDelay.DN)OTE(g_MachineBasic.MotionUpCP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[500ms Period Flasher (250 on / 250 off)

JARVIS INFERENCE: two-timer flasher pattern. 100ms and 250ms flashers follow the same pattern when needed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Flash500TimerB.DN)TON(Flash500TimerA,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Flash500TimerA.DN)TON(Flash500TimerB,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Flash500TimerA.DN)OTE(g_MachineBasic.Flash500msPD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.Flash500msPD)ONS(ONS.0)OTE(g_MachineBasic.Flash500msPS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[1s Period Flasher (500 on / 500 off)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Flash1sTimerB.DN)TON(Flash1sTimerA,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Flash1sTimerA.DN)TON(Flash1sTimerB,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Flash1sTimerA.DN)OTE(g_MachineBasic.Flash1sPD);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.Flash1sPD)ONS(ONS.1)OTE(g_MachineBasic.Flash1sPS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Controller Time And Date

Evidence: X-drive CPU_TimeDate_wJulian AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPU_TimeDate_wJulian(CPUDateTimeAOI,JulianDate,g_CPUDateTime);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R20_Alarms" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[***SUPERVISOR ALARMS***]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Safety Circuit Not OK]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(SafetyOK) XIC(g_MachineBasic.PowerUpCP) ,XIC(Alarm[0].Active) XIO(FaultReset) ][OTE(Alarm[0].Active) ,ONS(ONS.8) CONCAT(SupervisorPrefix,AlarmList[0],Alarm[0].Message) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Air Pressure Low]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(i_AirPressureOK) XIC(g_MachineBasic.PowerUpCP) ,XIC(Alarm[1].Active) XIO(FaultReset) ][OTE(Alarm[1].Active) ,ONS(ONS.9) CONCAT(SupervisorPrefix,AlarmList[1],Alarm[1].Message) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Machine Did Not Stop After Cycle Stop

JARVIS INFERENCE: warning (severity 1) - the machine keeps trying to stop; nothing is faulted. Machines that stop less: this alerts maintenance without adding a hard stop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Status.State[7])MOVE(30000,Control.FaultTime)XIC(Status.TimeoutFlt)[OTE(Alarm[2].Active) ,ONS(ONS.10) MOVE(1,Alarm[2].Severity) CONCAT(SupervisorPrefix,AlarmList[2],Alarm[2].Message) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Not Used]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOff)OTE(Alarm[3].Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Not Used]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOff)OTE(Alarm[4].Active);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Station Alarm Handler]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[ProgramAlarmHandler(ProgramFaultHandler,\Alarms.p_ProgramID,Alarm,\Alarms.p_Active,\Alarms.p_History,g_CPUDateTime,q_AlarmActive,q_WarningActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Use="Target" Name="Alarms" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Main" Disabled="false" Class="Standard" UseAsFolder="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[EVIDENCE-BASED - transcribed from the real SDC Alarms program export (X-drive, V2.2 era) with the station lineup updated to the V4.2 templates. p_ProgramID / p_Active / p_History are the shared arrays every ProgramAlarmHandler instance writes into.]]>
</Description>
<Tags>
<Tag Name="AlarmDataEmpty" TagType="Base" DataType="AlarmData" Constant="true" ExternalAccess="None" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Blank alarm record used to clear the active list]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="AlarmStop" TagType="Base" DataType="AlarmData" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[The fault that stopped the machine (V2.2)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="AlarmStopTrigger" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Pulse into TopAlarms when a machine-stopping fault is captured]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="DelayClose" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Alarm popup close delay]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,3000,0]]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="DisplayListPointer" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Alarm history scroll pointer]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="DispSize" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Size of HistoryDisplay]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HistoryDisplay" TagType="Base" DataType="AlarmData" Dimensions="16" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI window into the alarm history]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HistoryNav" TagType="Base" DataType="DisplayListControl" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI alarm history navigation buttons]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HistSize" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Size of p_History]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_ClearTopAlarms" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI - reset the top alarms lists]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="ONS" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One shot storage bits]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_Active" TagType="Base" DataType="AlarmData" Dimensions="16" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Shared active alarm list - newest at index 0]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_History" TagType="Base" DataType="AlarmData" Dimensions="50" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="None" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Shared alarm history - newest at index 0]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_NoMachineFaults" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[No faults anywhere on the machine]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_NoMachineWarnings" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[No warnings anywhere on the machine]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_ProgramID" TagType="Base" DataType="INT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="None" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Master program ID counter - zeroed here every scan, incremented by every ProgramAlarmHandler instance]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="TempPtrCheck" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Page-down pointer math helper]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="TopAlarms" TagType="Base" DataType="TopAlarmsDT" Dimensions="5" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Top 5 alarms since last reset (V2.2)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="TopAlarmsBacking" TagType="Base" DataType="TopAlarms" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[TopAlarms AOI backing tag]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="TopShiftAlarms" TagType="Base" DataType="TopAlarmsDT" Dimensions="3 5" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Top 5 alarms per shift, 3 shifts (V2.2)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Subroutine Calls]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R01_Logic,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R01_Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Evidence: this routine is transcribed from X:\...\Programs\Alarm\Alarms.L5X (the real SDC Alarms program), with the station fault/warning contact lineup updated from the pre-V4.0 naming (\StateMachine, \S03_PartLoad) to the four V4.2 template programs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(0,p_ProgramID);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[***MACHINE FAULTS***]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check for any machine faults present.

*Add one contact per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(\Supervisor.q_AlarmActive)XIO(\S00_IndexerSP.q_AlarmActive)XIO(\S01_PartLoad.q_AlarmActive)XIO(\S05_ServoPNP.q_AlarmActive)OTE(p_NoMachineFaults);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[***MACHINE WARNINGS***]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check For Any Machine Warnings Present

*Add one contact per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(\Supervisor.q_WarningActive)XIO(\S00_IndexerSP.q_WarningActive)XIO(\S01_PartLoad.q_WarningActive)XIO(\S05_ServoPNP.q_WarningActive)OTE(p_NoMachineWarnings);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Active Alarm list in case it has been corrupted via a PLC program download.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(S:FS) ,XIC(p_NoMachineWarnings) XIC(p_NoMachineFaults) ONS(ONS.5) ]COP(AlarmDataEmpty,p_Active[0],1)COP(p_Active[0],p_Active[1],15);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[***HMI ALARM HANDLING***
Logic for handling the alarm displays developed for the PV5500.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show Alarm popup when an alarm is present]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(p_NoMachineFaults)ONS(ONS.0)NE(\HMI.p_CurrentPopupNum,90)NE(\HMI.p_CurrentScreenNum,91)MOVE(90,\HMI.p_ReplaceScreenNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Close "Active Alarms" popup 90 or "All Active Alarms" screen 91 (If its showing) when there are no alarms present

Writing 9999 to \HMI.ReplaceScreenNum will close the pop up being displayed on the HMI
Writing 8888 to \HMI.ReplaceScreenNum will execute a NavBack command to return to previous screen on the HMI]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(p_NoMachineFaults) ,XIC(p_NoMachineWarnings) XIC(p_NoMachineFaults) ]TON(DelayClose,?,?)XIC(DelayClose.DN)ONS(ONS.1)[EQ(\HMI.p_CurrentPopupNum,90) MOVE(9999,\HMI.p_ReplaceScreenNum) ,EQ(\HMI.p_CurrentScreenNum,91) MOVE(8888,\HMI.p_ReplaceScreenNum) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Alarm History Display]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Array sizes

NOTE: the SDC standard uses SIZE(p_History[0],0,HistSize) and SIZE(HistoryDisplay[0],0,DispSize) here; constants are substituted only because this draft generator validates rung text against a fixed mnemonic set. Restore SIZE on import.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(S:FS)[MOVE(50,HistSize) ,MOVE(16,DispSize) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[History list navigation (PV5500 screen 99)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(\HMI.p_CurrentScreenNum,99)[ONS(ONS.2) MOVE(0,DisplayListPointer) ,XIC(HistoryNav.PageUp) ONS(ONS.3) [GE(DisplayListPointer,DispSize) CPT(DisplayListPointer,(DisplayListPointer+HistSize-DispSize-DispSize+1)MOD(HistSize-DispSize+1)) OTE(ONS.8) ,XIO(ONS.8) LT(DisplayListPointer,DispSize) MOVE(0,DisplayListPointer) ] ,XIC(HistoryNav.ScrollDown) ONS(ONS.4) CPT(DisplayListPointer,(DisplayListPointer+1)MOD(HistSize-DispSize+1)) ,XIC(HistoryNav.ScrollUp) ONS(ONS.6) CPT(DisplayListPointer,(DisplayListPointer+HistSize-DispSize)MOD(HistSize-DispSize+1)) ,XIC(HistoryNav.PageDown) ONS(ONS.7) CPT(TempPtrCheck,HistSize-DispSize-DispSize) [LT(DisplayListPointer,TempPtrCheck) CPT(DisplayListPointer,(DisplayListPointer+DispSize)MOD(HistSize-DispSize+1)) OTE(ONS.9) ,XIO(ONS.9) GE(DisplayListPointer,TempPtrCheck) CPT(DisplayListPointer,HistSize-DispSize) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIMIT(0,DisplayListPointer,HistSize)CMP((HistSize - DisplayListPointer) > DispSize)COP(p_History[DisplayListPointer],HistoryDisplay[0],DispSize);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Store Fault That Stopped The Machine]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(\Supervisor.q_MachineRunning)XIC(\Supervisor.q_MachineFaultActive)ONS(ONS.10)[XIC(p_Active[0].Active) EQ(p_Active[0].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[0],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[1].Active) EQ(p_Active[1].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[1],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[2].Active) EQ(p_Active[2].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[2],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[3].Active) EQ(p_Active[3].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[3],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[4].Active) EQ(p_Active[4].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[4],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[5].Active) EQ(p_Active[5].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[5],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[6].Active) EQ(p_Active[6].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[6],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[7].Active) EQ(p_Active[7].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[7],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[8].Active) EQ(p_Active[8].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[8],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[9].Active) EQ(p_Active[9].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[9],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[10].Active) EQ(p_Active[10].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[10],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[11].Active) EQ(p_Active[11].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[11],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[12].Active) EQ(p_Active[12].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[12],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[13].Active) EQ(p_Active[13].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[13],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[14].Active) EQ(p_Active[14].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[14],AlarmStop,1) ,XIC(p_Active[15].Active) EQ(p_Active[15].Severity,0) COP(p_Active[15],AlarmStop,1) ,OTE(AlarmStopTrigger) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Store Top 5 Alarms Since Reset & Per Shift]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[TopAlarms(TopAlarmsBacking,AlarmStop,AlarmStopTrigger,TopAlarms,TopShiftAlarms,\Production.p_CurrentShift,HMI_ClearTopAlarms,3);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Use="Target" Name="Tracking" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Main" Disabled="false" Class="Standard" UseAsFolder="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[JARVIS DRAFT - part tracking data owner (p_Data / p_NestQty), operator status distribution (Lockout/DryRun/SingleStep per station), nest record lifecycle, batch counter. Added in V4.0 but never exported; the p_Data structure is reverse-engineered from every station access path, everything else is JARVIS INFERENCE.]]>
</Description>
<Tags>
<Tag Name="p_Data" TagType="Base" DataType="TrackingData" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Machine part tracking data - Station[] indexed by StaNum, Nest[] indexed by nest number. Structure reverse-engineered from every station template access path.]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_NestQty" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Number of nests on the dial. Used by S00 R10 as the modulo base for nest numbering. JARVIS INFERENCE: 20 nests matches the S01 template StaNumPre=20 wraparound.]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[20]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="q_GoodPartPulse" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One-scan pulse per good part unloaded - Production program good part trigger]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="q_RejectPartPulse" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One-scan pulse per rejected part - Production program reject part trigger]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="q_BatchComplete" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Batch target reached - Supervisor unlatches the cycle (stop reason 5)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_StationLockout" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI toggles - bit number = station number - lock out a station]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_StationDryRun" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI toggles - bit number = station number - dry run a station]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_StationSingleStep" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI toggles - bit number = station number - single step a station]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_NestLockout" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI toggles - bit number = nest number - lock out a nest (cleanout)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_BatchTarget" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Batch size target - 0 disables the batch counter]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_BatchReset" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI - reset the batch count]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="BatchCount" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Good parts produced in the current batch]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="LoadStaNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Station number of the load station]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[1]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="UnloadStaNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="true" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Station number of the final/unload station. *Set to the real unload station (S18/S19 on a full machine); 5 = S05 in this three-station draft.]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[5]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="UnloadNestNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Nest currently at the unload station]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="NestAtLoadPrev" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Nest number at the load station on the previous scan]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="NestsShifted" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One-scan pulse when the dial has indexed (nest at load changed)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="PartStatusEmpty" TagType="Base" DataType="TrackingPartStatus" Constant="true" ExternalAccess="None" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Blank part status record used to clear a nest]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="ONS" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One shot storage bits]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Subroutine Calls]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R01_OpStatus,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R02_PartData,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R03_BatchCounter,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R01_OpStatus" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Operator Status Distribution

JARVIS INFERENCE: the V4.2 stations read Lockout/DryRun/SingleStep from \Tracking.p_Data.Station[StaNum].OpStatus (this replaced the old HMI_Toggle word in each station). Something must SET those bits - this routine maps per-function HMI toggle words (bit = station number) onto the OpStatus structure. The real mechanism (per-station HMI buttons writing the bits directly?) is unconfirmed.

*Add one rung per station program]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[S00 Indexer Operator Status - single step only (the indexer has no Lockout or DryRun)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_StationSingleStep.0)OTE(p_Data.Station[0].OpStatus.SingleStep);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[S01 Part Load Operator Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(HMI_StationLockout.1) OTE(p_Data.Station[1].OpStatus.Lockout) ,XIC(HMI_StationDryRun.1) OTE(p_Data.Station[1].OpStatus.DryRun) ,XIC(HMI_StationSingleStep.1) OTE(p_Data.Station[1].OpStatus.SingleStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[S05 Servo PNP Operator Status]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(HMI_StationLockout.5) OTE(p_Data.Station[5].OpStatus.Lockout) ,XIC(HMI_StationDryRun.5) OTE(p_Data.Station[5].OpStatus.DryRun) ,XIC(HMI_StationSingleStep.5) OTE(p_Data.Station[5].OpStatus.SingleStep) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nest Lockout (cleanout)

JARVIS INFERENCE: per-nest lockout consumed by the S01 Cycle Station rung. Example rung for nest 1 - *add one per nest, or replace with indexed MOV logic.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_NestLockout.1)OTE(p_Data.Nest[1].OpStatus.Lockout);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R02_PartData" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nest Data Ownership

Evidence boundary: stations only LATCH Attempt/Success/Lockout/PartLoaded bits and S00 only writes Station[].NestNum. Nothing in any template ever CLEARS a nest record - so the Tracking program must own clearing. Everything below is JARVIS INFERENCE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Nest At Unload Station]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(p_Data.Station[UnloadStaNum].NestNum,UnloadNestNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Good Part Pulse - part completed the unload station successfully]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p_Data.Nest[UnloadNestNum].PartStatus.Station[UnloadStaNum].Success)ONS(ONS.0)OTE(q_GoodPartPulse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reject Part Pulse]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(p_Data.Nest[UnloadNestNum].PartStatus.Station[UnloadStaNum].Failure)ONS(ONS.1)OTE(q_RejectPartPulse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Detect Dial Index - nest number at the load station changed

JARVIS INFERENCE: S00 R10 computes a NestsShiftedPulse locally but never publishes it; Tracking re-derives the same pulse from the NestNum it owns.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(p_Data.Station[LoadStaNum].NestNum,NestAtLoadPrev)[OTE(NestsShifted) ,MOVE(p_Data.Station[LoadStaNum].NestNum,NestAtLoadPrev) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear Nest Record When A Finished Nest Arrives Back At The Load Station

JARVIS INFERENCE - QUESTION FOR LEADS: where does the standard clear Nest[].PartStatus? This draft clears it when the nest re-arrives at load with its part already unloaded (Success, Failure, or Lockout at the unload station). An incomplete part (attempted but never unloaded) is deliberately NOT cleared so the record survives a fault recovery - machines that stop less.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(NestsShifted)XIC(p_Data.Nest[NestAtLoadPrev].PartStatus.PartLoaded)[XIC(p_Data.Nest[NestAtLoadPrev].PartStatus.Station[UnloadStaNum].Success) ,XIC(p_Data.Nest[NestAtLoadPrev].PartStatus.Station[UnloadStaNum].Failure) ,XIC(p_Data.Nest[NestAtLoadPrev].PartStatus.Station[UnloadStaNum].Lockout) ]COP(PartStatusEmpty,p_Data.Nest[NestAtLoadPrev].PartStatus,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R03_BatchCounter" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Batch Counter (added V4.1)

JARVIS INFERENCE: the revision history says only "Added batch counter" - which program owns it is unconfirmed. Placed in Tracking because it counts tracked parts. Batch complete requests a cycle stop through the Supervisor unlatch rung (stop reason 5) rather than faulting anything - machines that stop less.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Count Good Parts Into The Batch]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(q_GoodPartPulse)ADD(BatchCount,1,BatchCount);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Batch Complete]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GT(HMI_BatchTarget,0)GE(BatchCount,HMI_BatchTarget)OTE(q_BatchComplete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Batch Reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_BatchReset)MOVE(0,BatchCount);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Use="Target" Name="HMI" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Main" Disabled="false" Class="Standard" UseAsFolder="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[EVIDENCE-BASED - transcribed from the real SDC HMI program export (X-drive). Screen/popup arbitration for the PV5500. Adds q_CleanoutModeEnabled (referenced by the V4.2 S01 template but missing from the older X-drive export).]]>
</Description>
<Tags>
<Tag Name="OneShot" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[One shot storage bits]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="PopupHidden" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Popup commanded to open but is already open, probably hidden in the background.]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_CurrentPopupNum" TagType="Base" DataType="INT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Current Popup Number Viewed On The HMI]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[90]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_CurrentScreenNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Current Screen Number Viewed On The HMI]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[1]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_PreviousScreenNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[1]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="p_ReplaceScreenNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Public" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Screen to open on HMI. 9999 - close popup. 8888 - previous]]>
</Description>
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[0]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="QueuedPopupNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
</Tag>
<Tag Name="q_ScreenChangedOneShot" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
</Tag>
<Tag Name="ResendCurrentPopup" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,550,0]]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="ResetReplaceScreen" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,2000,0]]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="SavedPopupNum" TagType="Base" DataType="DINT" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[90]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="HMI_CleanoutMode" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[HMI toggle - cleanout mode (run parts out without loading new ones)]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="q_CleanoutModeEnabled" TagType="Base" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Usage="Output" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read Only" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Cleanout mode active - S01 skips loading new parts]]>
</Description>
</Tag>
</Tags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="R00_Main" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Subroutine Calls]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JSR(R01_Logic,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="R01_Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Evidence: transcribed from X:\...\Programs\HMI\HMI.L5X (the real SDC HMI program). Only the cleanout rung at the end is new.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Screen Change]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(p_CurrentScreenNum,p_PreviousScreenNum)[MOVE(p_CurrentScreenNum,p_PreviousScreenNum) ,OTE(q_ScreenChangedOneShot) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Main screen handshaking]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(p_ReplaceScreenNum,p_CurrentScreenNum)MOVE(0,p_ReplaceScreenNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[popup handshaking]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(p_ReplaceScreenNum,0)ONS(OneShot.0)EQ(p_ReplaceScreenNum,p_CurrentPopupNum)OTE(PopupHidden);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Popup request to open but there's already one open.
Save the screen number and open it when the current popup closes.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(p_ReplaceScreenNum,0)ONS(OneShot.1)LIMIT(80,p_ReplaceScreenNum,90)NE(p_ReplaceScreenNum,p_CurrentPopupNum)NE(p_CurrentPopupNum,0)[MOVE(p_ReplaceScreenNum,QueuedPopupNum) ,MOVE(0,p_ReplaceScreenNum) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(p_ReplaceScreenNum,p_CurrentPopupNum)MOVE(0,p_ReplaceScreenNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Current popup isn't being shown if the screen changes.
 (assuming only 1 HMI screen)
So force the popup back up by
closing it and resending it.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(q_ScreenChangedOneShot) ,XIC(PopupHidden) ] NE(p_CurrentPopupNum,0) [MOVE(p_CurrentPopupNum,SavedPopupNum) ,MOVE(9999,p_ReplaceScreenNum) ] ,XIC(ResendCurrentPopup.TT) XIO(ResendCurrentPopup.DN) ]TON(ResendCurrentPopup,?,?)XIC(ResendCurrentPopup.DN)MOVE(SavedPopupNum,p_ReplaceScreenNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[GT(QueuedPopupNum,0)EQ(p_CurrentPopupNum,0)[MOVE(QueuedPopupNum,p_ReplaceScreenNum) ,MOVE(0,QueuedPopupNum) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Prevent replace screen num from getting stuck.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQ(p_ReplaceScreenNum,9999) ,EQ(p_ReplaceScreenNum,8888) ]TON(ResetReplaceScreen,?,?)XIC(ResetReplaceScreen.DN)MOVE(0,p_ReplaceScreenNum);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cleanout Mode

JARVIS INFERENCE: q_CleanoutModeEnabled is referenced by S01 (skip loading new parts so the dial runs empty) but the X-drive HMI export predates it. Gating on the cycle being latched OFF for enable is NOT assumed - cleanout runs WITH the cycle so parts flow out. Leads: confirm any interlock.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(HMI_CleanoutMode)OTE(q_CleanoutModeEnabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
<Program Use="Target" Name="Production" TestEdits="false" MainRoutineName="R00_Main" Disabled="false" Class="Standard" UseAsFolder="false">
<Description>
<![CDATA[EVIDENCE-BASED - transcribed from the real SDC Production program export (X-drive, pre-V4.1) with the V4.1 revision-history changes applied and marked. Good/Reject triggers wired to the Tracking program pulses per the ***Replace*** notes in the original.]]>
</Description>
<Tags>
<Tag Name="CycleDowntime" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,1000,0]]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="CycleRuntime" TagType="Base" DataType="TIMER" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Data Format="L5K">
<![CDATA[[0,1000,0]]]>
</Data>
</Tag>
<Tag Name="EmptyData" TagType="Base" DataType="ProductionData" Constant="false" ExternalAccess="Read/Write" OpcUaAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Blank record for count resets]]>
